# Separation of Concerns

If you cram everything into `Update()`, it becomes a monster. Instead, break logic into methods:

```csharp
void Update()
{
    HandleInput();
    MovePlayer();
    CheckCollisions();
}
```

Each method does one specific job. This makes debugging a breeze.
